# Code owners for this repository.
#
# GitHub requests a review from the owner of every path a pull request touches.
# Rules are gitignore-style patterns; the LAST matching rule wins, so the
# catch-all comes first and the narrower rules below only re-state it.
#
# There is one maintainer today, so every rule names the same person. They are
# written out anyway: these are the paths where a missing review is expensive
# (they can publish a release, mint a token, or change what the gate lets
# through), so if ownership is ever widened, widening it has to be a deliberate
# edit to the catch-all rather than something these paths inherit silently.

# Everything, unless a later rule says otherwise.
*                                    @baliutkarsh2

# CI, release automation, the published composite Action, and the images. A
# change here can run arbitrary code with the repository's credentials.
/.github/                            @baliutkarsh2
/action.yml                          @baliutkarsh2
/Dockerfile                          @baliutkarsh2
/docker-compose.yml                  @baliutkarsh2

# Supply chain: what gets built, what gets installed, and what ships in the
# wheel. A wrong line here reaches every user through PyPI.
/pyproject.toml                      @baliutkarsh2
/MANIFEST.in                         @baliutkarsh2
/.pre-commit-config.yaml             @baliutkarsh2

# Security-relevant surfaces: the disclosure policy, the secret scanner config,
# the synthetic-credential fixtures, the TLS-terminating intercept proxy, and
# the dashboard's auth middleware.
/SECURITY.md                         @baliutkarsh2
/.gitleaks.toml                      @baliutkarsh2
/checkpoint/fake_credentials.py      @baliutkarsh2
/checkpoint/proxy/                   @baliutkarsh2
/checkpoint/dashboard/middleware.py  @baliutkarsh2

# Licensing: Apache-2.0 plus the NOTICE file the licence obliges downstream
# redistributors to carry.
/LICENSE                             @baliutkarsh2
/NOTICE                              @baliutkarsh2
